        <h3>Why Standard Online Image Resizers Fail at 10KB</h3>
        <p>
          Most basic compression tools utilize simple quality sliders (such as 50% or 30%). When applied to an uncropped 4K resolution image:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Overhead Bloat Remains:</strong> Camera headers, EXIF color profiles, thumbnail caches, and GPS coordinates remain embedded, consuming 8KB to 24KB alone—exceeding your entire budget before image pixel data is even evaluated.</li>
          <li><strong>Extreme Color Banding:</strong> Simple encoders drop the color quantization tables uniformly. This leaves dark ink strokes on white signatures looking fuzzy, broken, or washed out.</li>
          <li><strong>No Dimensional Downsampling:</strong> Attempting to squeeze 4000x3000 pixels into a 10KB payload forces the JPEG encoder to average pixels across giant 8x8 blocks, destroying fine text or lines.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          ConvertKB avoids these traps. Our tool automatically scales the canvas resolution to appropriate dimensions (e.g., 200–400px width), strips all extraneous metadata tags, and optimizes black-and-white ink boundaries.
        </p>

